America/Winnipeg moves to permanent UTC-5 on 31 October 2026. IANA 2026e models
this as standard time after its temporary CLDR workaround ends in November.
Represent it instead as UTC-6 plus one hour of permanent DST, keeping the
America_Central metazone and Central Daylight Time display name. Linked zones,
including Canada/Central and America/Rainy_River, inherit the same rules.

Retain the distant abbreviation transition used for Vancouver and Edmonton:
CDT changes to the invented CenT on 8 March 2100 without changing the UTC
offset or DST state. This preserves compatibility with Android implementations
that lack the ZoneInfoData permanent DST fix, even though this checkout already
has that fix. libc can expose CenT for timestamps after that distant transition;
Java and ICU formatting APIs continue to use CLDR's Central Daylight Time name.

See 002-northamerica.info.
